rule: TEST_DISABLED
issue: 419
title: a guarded hook beside an opaque production edit holds at warn by its own gate, not by the opaque edit
origin: #209 B9 (ruling 209.Q4): only an unguarded control refuses repair
origin2: evidence (D-028), as B10's collect_ignore did. Since #419 that reading no longer covers opaque
origin3: evidence, which is refused for any TEST_DISABLED in a Python conftest, guarded or not.
origin4: Re-pinned by the #419 ruling (issuecomment-6170353038: Q1 (b), rule 2): TEST_DISABLED in a
origin5: Python conftest refuses opaque-change evidence, guarded or not. The NETWORK guard is a compat
origin6: gate (D6, as in conftest_hook_env_guard_neg), so the finding holds at warn through COMPAT_GATE:
origin7: same severity, same verdict, a different reason.
